Negative control for the wrapper's `:optional-text` seam.

Drops the binding that hands the engine the catalogue's wording for the
optional marker. Without it the engine falls back to its own English,
which is invisible to an English-locale test unless the assertion pins a
sentinel -- which is why the assertion overrides `text.optional`.

MUST red: optional copy > "marks an optional control with the
catalogue's own wording". The bare-engine twin MUST stay green.
